  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parophromenus-sumatranus",
      "html": "<p>One of the more commonly available Parosphromenus species. Similar to some species with brown/dark red unpaired fins. Distinguished from Parosphromenus bintan and P. deissneri by a conspicuous black spot at the posterior extremity of the dorsal-fin base (absent in those species). Differs from P. bintan in having a black pelvic fin filament (white in P. bintan).</p><p>Size: up to 3.5 cm for males.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parophromenus-sumatranus",
      "html": "<ul><li>Temperature: 22–28 °C</li><li>pH: 3.0–6.5</li><li>Hardness: 18–72 ppm</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parophromenus-sumatranus",
      "html": "<p>They are carnivores, feeding on a variety of small invertebrates and insect larvae. They will ONLY eat live food!</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parophromenus-sumatranus",
      "html": "<p>These fish are generally peaceful and shy, preferring to hide among vegetation or other structures in their environment.</p>"
    }
